                <pb facs="0967" n="849" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg849"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.4061/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-05-04T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1928—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>124. Your 111, May 2, 3 p.m. Department cordially approves such informal
                    conciliatory efforts by Embassy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
